From snow at fisher.byu.edu  Tue Apr  3 16:32:49 2001
From: snow at fisher.byu.edu (Greg Snow)
Date: Tue, 03 Apr 2001 10:32:49 -0600
Subject: A little function to help understand loess
In-Reply-To: <sac9e8a1.087@wpo.nerc.ac.uk>
References: <sac9e8a1.087@wpo.nerc.ac.uk>
Message-ID: <Pine.GSO.4.21.0104031018580.6799-100000@fisher.byu.edu>

Loess is a powerful smoother, but sometimes is hard to understand and even
harder to explain to someone else.  Below is a function that I wrote for
S-PLUS 2000 (may work in other versions, but I have not tested it) to help
me understand what is going on with loess.  It only shows 1 predictor
problems, try it out by loading it into S-PLUS then typeing:

attach(ethanol)
loess.demo(E, NOx, span=.5)

It starts with a scatterplot and loess smooth, if you click on the plot
then it will show you how the estimate for the x-value that you clicked on
is generated.  The window of points actually used will be shown and each
point in the window will have a circle around it with the area of the
circle proportional to the weight that that point gets, points outside the
window without circles get 0 weight.  It also shows the weighted line and
the prediction at the x value you clicked on.  The smooth, the weighted
line, and the vertical line indicating the x-value being predicted should
all cross at the same point, the prediction (occasionally they don't, I
think because of rounding differences and extra interpolation done by
S-PLUS, but it gives the right idea).

Click on another point to see how that one is estimated.  Right click to
end the demo.  

I make no guarentees (some parts were a result of trial and error), but it
has worked so far for me.

I hope it helps others,

loess.demo<-function(x, y, span = 2/3, xlim, ylim)
{
  # function to demonstrate the locally weighted regression function loess
  # written by Dr. Greg Snow 
  # Brigham Young University, Department of Statistics
  # gls at byu.edu
  tmp <- loess.smooth(x, y, span, family = "gaussian")
  xl <- range(x, tmp$x)
  xl <- xl + c(-1, 1) * 0.03 * diff(xl)
  yl <- range(y, tmp$y)
  yl <- yl + c(-1, 1) * 0.05 * diff(yl)
  scatter.smooth(x, y, span, xlab = "x", ylab = "y", pch = ".", xlim = xl,
    ylim = yl, family = "gaussian")
  repeat {
    x0 <- locator(1)$x
    if(length(x0) < 1)
      break
    if( span < 1 ){
      q <- as.integer(span * length(x))
      d <- sort(abs(x - x0))[q]
    } else {
      d <- max( abs(x - x0) ) * sqrt(span)
    }
    w <- rep(0, length(x))
    s <- abs(x - x0) <= d
    w[s] <- (1 - (abs(x[s] - x0)/d)^3)^3
    scatter.smooth(x, y, span, xlab = "x", ylab = "y", pch =".", 
      xlim = xl, ylim = yl, family = "gaussian")
    symbols(x, y, circle = sqrt(w), inches = 0.3, add = T, col= 6)
    abline(lsfit(x, y, w), col = 5)
    abline(v = x0, col = 5)
    if(x0 - d > xl[1])
      abline(v = x0 - d, col = 5, lty = 2)
    if(x0 + d < xl[2])
      abline(v = x0 + d, col = 5, lty = 2)
  }
}

