offering of "Environmental Statistics with S-PLUS". 
This course will be presented by Dr Steven Millard, author 
of the S+Environmental Statistics add-on module. This 2-day 
course covers basic and advanced concepts in environmental 
statistical design and analysis, and shows how to apply these 
concepts in practice using S-PLUS and the add-in module 
EnvironmentalStats for S-PLUS. 
The course includes both lecture and hands-on instruction, 
with each student using a PC to implement examples and exercises. 
Each student will receive a set of course notes, as well as the 
textbook "Environmental Statistics with S-PLUS" published by CRC Press.

Presenter Info:
Dr. Steven P. Millard is Manager of Consulting Services at 
Insightful, and the creator of EnvironmentalStats for S-PLUS 
(an S-PLUS add-in module for environmental statistics and risk 
assessment). He has been involved in the field of environmental 
statistics for 20 years, including working on the second Love Canal 
Habitability study, acting as an expert witness for litigation on 
water quality in the Everglades, and teaching statistics courses for 
the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency. Dr. Millard has worked for 
the U.S. Geological Survey, CH2M Hill, the University of California 
at Santa Barbara, the University of Washington, and Statistical Sciences

(now part of Insightful), where he launched the training program in
S-PLUS. 
Dr. Millard has authored and co-authored several articles on the
application 
of environmental statistics, and is the principal co-author of the
textbook 
