From thacker at aoml.noaa.gov  Thu Apr  5 17:35:48 2001
From: thacker at aoml.noaa.gov (Carlisle Thacker)
Date: Thu, 05 Apr 2001 13:35:48 -0400
Subject: unlisting data frames
In-Reply-To: <01Apr4.105112wst.119046@firewall.fish.wa.gov.au>
References: <01Apr4.105112wst.119046@firewall.fish.wa.gov.au>
Message-ID: <Pine.GSO.4.03.10104051326180.1416-100000@ahab>

Splusers,

Is there an easy and fast way to collapse a list that contains data
frames into a single data frame?

Using a for loop is very slow, probably because it reads from and
writes to disk in each pass.  For example, if A is a long list, each
element of which is a data frame with same sort of data, the desired
data frame is B, where:
   B <- NULL
   for (i in 1:length(A)) B <- rbind(B,A[[i]])

Thanks,

Carlisle

