From Mike.Prager at noaa.gov  Thu Apr  5 19:12:00 2001
From: Mike.Prager at noaa.gov (Mike Prager)
Date: Thu, 05 Apr 2001 15:12:00 -0400
Subject: Cookbook available?
Message-ID: <5.0.2.1.2.20010405145704.00ad2e70@nsmail.ccfhrb.noaa.gov>

Is an S-Plus "cookbook" available anywhere?  By that I mean a task-oriented 
compilation of common S-Plus idioms.  If not, have any authors out there 
considered writing one?

The thought was inspired by David Kane's recent question:

> I often have dataframes with many factor variables that are subsets of much

> larger dataframes. Many of the levels of the factors are not present in the

> subset. I would like to remove them.  ...  But is there a way to do this 
for

> all the factor variables in a given dataframe in one pass, without knowing

> ahead of time which variables are present and which are factors?

and Brian Ripley's answer answer:

subsetDF[] <- lapply(subsetDF, function(x) if(is.factor(x)) x[drop=T] else x)

They seem to illustrate perfectly the type of problem that is reasonably 
common, not trivial for a new user to solve, and the solution of which is 
generalizable to similar problems -- all fine criteria for such a volume.

Much of the existing documentation seems to be organized by function name, 
rather than task accomplished, and to be more focused on specification of 
calls ather than on application to get something done.  A cookbook could be 
a big help to those of us who respond to a more concrete approach.  I would 
like to see it on my shelf next to the various versions of V&R, the 
"Insightful" documentation, and Chambers' book.

--
