Subject: Tree Object- explained variance
Message-ID: <6B677297622ED311A8E100902785F9310302A380@ribes.for.orst.edu>

Hi all,
I have a function that returns the explained variance for an entire tree
object.  I would like to also return the explained variance for each
split/node of my tree object.  I'd also like to return explained variances
through the graphing options offered by post.tree.   

Here's the explained variance function:

 deviance.explained <-
function(fit)
{
        1 - (deviance.tree(fit)/sum((fit$y - mean(fit$y))^2))
}

Any suggestions for functions that could accomplish my objectives would be
appreciated.

Thank you,
Michael Wing

