Date: Thu, 05 Apr 2001 17:35:30 -0400
Subject: Summary for Removing unused factor levels from a subset of a dataframe
Message-ID: <15052.57836.644375.215731@arbres2a>

Thanks to David Smith, Don MacQueen, Todd Hatfield, Frank Harrell, Sean Keenan
and Brain Ripley for taking the time to answer my question.

I have ended up using the following incantation at the top of most functions
(with an arguement df for the input dataframe).

  df <- data.frame(lapply(df, "[", drop = T))

This seems to work fine. Special thanks to David Smith. Professor Ripley
suggested something similar:

subsetDF[] <- lapply(subsetDF, function(x) if(is.factor(x)) x[drop=T] else x)

I *think* that these two approaches are identical since, according to David
Smith, the drop = T does no harm to non-factor variables in the dataframe.

Several people suggested Frank Harrell's most excellent Hmisc library.

Thanks again,

