Some general opinions -

Stepwise techniques are not "model fitting" methods, depending on
what you mean by "fitting".  Stepwise regression is an exploratory
but highly unstable method.  Spending time developing a tentative
model based on subject matter knowledge (only) will pay off.

The dependent variable needs no transformation.

Dimensionality reduction can help.  Roughly speaking a ratio
of 15 observations in the least frequent outcome category (in
the two category case) per degree of freedom ever examined
(formally or informally) against the response variable
will result in a reliable model in
terms of future performance.

You might look at 

@ARTICLE{har84,
  author = {Harrell, F. E. and Lee, K. L. and Califf, R. M. and Pryor,
D. B.
           and Rosati, R. A.},
  year = 1984,
  title = {Regression modeling strategies for improved prognostic
prediction},
  journal = Stat in Med,
  volume = 3,
  pages = {143-152}
}

