From vukov at avaya.com  Tue Apr 10 22:53:53 2001
From: vukov at avaya.com (Vukov, Suzanne (Suzan))
Date: Tue, 10 Apr 2001 18:53:53 -0400
Subject: ANSWER: how to substitute values w/ passed parms [UNIX]
Message-ID: <CB69DF10FAAB0140926EC2F82B7F118FAB37D0@NEOH00AVEXU1.global.avaya.com>

This news group is the best thing and Barry (Baz) Rowlingson pulled through again.

See response below.

Original question part of e-mail w/ subject line: [S] coercing character data on importData

> ***** 2nd Question:

> Thanks to Baz Rowlingson and Don MacQueen, I am passing some values

> via environment variables.  I have successfully used these parameters

> with paste

> 

> but I gather it is not always a simple case of substitution.

> For example:

>         uom <-getenv("SPLUS_UOM")

>                 uom will be either "dB" or "mV"

>         sink(statsum)

>         summary(uom)

> 

>              sink()

> 

> Result in statsum is:   Length    Class           Mode

>                         1               character

> Again...what am I missing?

 uom is the character string 'dB' or 'mV'. Thats why you are getting

a summary that says length 1 character.

 I suspect you want the summary of the object called dB or mV. The way

to do it is to use the 'get' function on the character variable with the

name in it:

 uom <- "mV"

 get(uom)

   will return the object mV, hence:

 summary(get(uom))

