From svrontos at aueb.gr  Wed Apr 11 22:55:10 2001
From: svrontos at aueb.gr (Spyros Vrontos)
Date: Thu, 12 Apr 2001 01:55:10 +0300
Subject: Summary of how to split a data frame.
Message-ID: <3.0.3.32.20010412015510.006aa59c@aueb.gr>

Hi all.
Many thanks to Gibiansky Leonid, Gerrit Eichner,
Renaud Lancelot, Ed Jones, Carlisle Thacker and David L Lorenz.

The question was how to split a data frame like:

v1 <- c(rep(c("A", "B", "C"), 5), "A") ; v2 <- 1:16
dat1 <- as.data.frame(cbind(v1, v2)) 

according to the levels of variable v1,
and save each piece as a data frame.

The answers are:

1. dat1 <- split(dat1,group=dat1$v1)
 
2. split(dat1, dat1$v1) 

3. by(dat1, dat1$v1, function(x)x)

4. dat.A <- dat1[dat1$v1=="A",] , for each level A,B,C.

Thanks a lot.

