On Tue, 17 Apr 2001, Sameer Savla wrote:

> Hi all,
>
> SPlus has a function called cut.dates which can covert dates into weeks,
> months, years etc, but not into quarters. Does anyone know of a simple way
> to do quarters?

Actually, cut.dates is from library chron, and applies to chron-like dates
(there being other date formats in S-PLUS).

It depends on your definition of `quarters'.  If you mean calendar 3-month
periods (and the term comes from something else in the English legal
system), convert the dates to the illogical month.day.year, discard the
days, group the months and then use factor.

As in

x <- seq.dates("01/01/92", "12/31/92", by="months")
xx <- month.day.year(as.vector(x))[-2]
xxx <- paste(xx$year, (xx$month+2)%/%3, sep="Q")
factor(xxx)

