On Wed, 18 Apr 2001, Bertrand Villeneuve wrote:

> Hi everybody,
>
> I perform linear models with 7 predictors using the linear regression 
> fonction.
> One of these predictor is new and when I try to perform the new model Splus
> gives me that message:
>
> "Error in lm.fit.qr(x, y): computed fit is singular, rank 13
> Dumped"
>
> What does it means?
> The old model is OK and I can't find what is the matter with the new one.

If you fit with singular.ok=TRUE it will tell you the problem by setting
one coefficient to NA.  The problem is collinearity, often caused by some
group not occurring in the data, or some factor levels only occurring
together.

