From dsmith at insightful.com  Wed Apr 18 18:17:25 2001
From: dsmith at insightful.com (David M Smith)
Date: Wed, 18 Apr 2001 11:17:25 -0700
Subject: Re: To Generate graphics file for word
In-Reply-To: <3ADDBA53.B315BE2A@cirad.fr>
References: <3ADDBA53.B315BE2A@cirad.fr>
Message-ID: <LGEFIDJJDBKMHCAKBCOIAELECPAA.dsmith@insightful.com>

You don't mention which version of S-PLUS you are using, but with the
Windows version (since you're using Word, I guess that's what you're using)
you can pass an image table (with interpolated colours between up to 5
points in RGB space) to the graphsheet() function:

> graphsheet(image.color.table="0,0,0|255,255,255",
num.image.colors=2,num.image.shades=2)
> X <- matrix(sample(1:4,400,rep=T),ncol=20)
> image(X)

Here we have 2 (num.image.shades) greys between the 2 (num.image.colors)
points black (0,0,0) and white (255,55,55).

On other platforms you can use postscript() and the colors and image.colors
arguments to ps.options().

