From a296180 at mica.fmr.com  Thu Apr 19 12:26:32 2001
From: a296180 at mica.fmr.com (David Kane - GEODE <David Kane)
Date: Thu, 19 Apr 2001 08:26:32 -0400
Subject: Correction to Determining the last day of the month
Message-ID: <15070.55179.934923.119442@arbres2a>

Thanks to Bill Dunlap and Nick Ellis for further suggestions. Special thanks to
Leonid Gibiansky and Robert Platt for pointing out that my previous summary was
in error. It fails for December:

> version
Version 6.0 Release 1 for Sun SPARC, SunOS 5.6 : 2000 
> mm <- 8
> yyyy <- 1998
> timeCalendar(m=mm%%12+1, y=yyyy, d=1) -1
[1] 08/31/1998                                  # Correct.      
> mm <- 12
> timeCalendar(m=mm%%12+1, y=yyyy, d=1) -1
[1] 12/31/1997                                  # Wrong. Should be 12/31/1998

Im the end, I went with the following (as part of a larger program):

mm.next <- mm + 1
mm   <- ifelse(mm.next == 13,        1, mm + 1)
yyyy <- ifelse(mm.next == 13, yyyy + 1, yyyy)   
result <- timeCalendar(m = mm, y = yyyy, d = 1) - 1

This handles vectors for mm and yyyy as well. Thanks again for all the
suggestions.

Dave Kane

